{"name":"Comfort","hex":"#e3ceb8","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Comfort","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname.","A female given name."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Comfort"}],"entries":[{"title":"Comfort","blocks":[{"text":"Comfort is a state of physical or psychological ease, often characterized by the absence of hardship. Individuals experiencing a lack of comfort are typically described as uncomfortable or in discomfort. A degree of psychological comfort can be achieved by recreating experiences that are associated with pleasant memories, such as engaging in familiar activities, maintaining the presence of familiar objects, and consumption of comfort foods. Comfort is a particular concern in health care, as providing comfort to the sick and injured is one goal of healthcare, and can facilitate recovery. The phrase \"comfort zone\" is sometimes used to describe a psychological state associated with perceived safety and familiarity. Because of the personal nature of positive associations, psychological comfort is highly subjective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/This_dog_is_%22comfy%22-_2013-12-27_10-51.jpg/330px-This_dog_is_%22comfy%22-_2013-12-27_10-51.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Comfort","wikidata":"Q1367353"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Rama_comforts_Sita.jpg/500px-Rama_comforts_Sita.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Rama_comforts_Sita.jpg/500px-Rama_comforts_Sita.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Rama comforts Sita","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARama_comforts_Sita.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Well-clothed_baby.jpg/500px-Well-clothed_baby.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Well-clothed_baby.jpg/1280px-Well-clothed_baby.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Well-clothed_baby.jpg/500px-Well-clothed_baby.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A baby wearing many items of winter clothing: headband, cap, fur-lined coat, scarf and sweater","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWell-clothed_baby.jpg"}],"sounds":{},"pictures":[{"title":"Grey heron (00129p)","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Grey_heron_%2800129p%29.jpg/500px-Grey_heron_%2800129p%29.jpg","ratio":0.8691693290734824,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grey_heron_(00129p).jpg","share":0.51375},{"title":"Comfort, Tex (26320988042)","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Comfort%2C_Tex_%2826320988042%29.jpg/500px-Comfort%2C_Tex_%2826320988042%29.jpg","ratio":1.5492957746478873,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Comfort,_Tex_(26320988042).jpg","share":0.399375},{"title":"USNS Comfort Baltimore 2012","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/USNS_Comfort_Baltimore_2012.jpg/500px-USNS_Comfort_Baltimore_2012.jpg","ratio":1.4255230125523013,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:USNS_Comfort_Baltimore_2012.jpg","share":0.270625},{"title":"USNS Comfort (49673237438)","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/USNS_Comfort_%2849673237438%29.jpg/500px-USNS_Comfort_%2849673237438%29.jpg","ratio":1.7778303001654456,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:USNS_Comfort_(49673237438).jpg","share":0.199375},{"title":"USN Comfort approaching Pier 90 in NYC","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/USN_Comfort_appro